# Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream [010051F0207B2000] v1.0.4 - Disable FXAA

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the FXAA post-process anti-aliasing pass in agl::pfx::FilterAA::draw.
// The filter dispatches on its antialias_type field (this+0x748): 0 = FXAA,
// 1 = ReduceAA, 2 = SMAA. ReduceAA/SMAA are left intact if ever selected.
//
// This game runs FXAA in place: the pass's source texture is the color buffer
// it renders to. Redirecting FXAA to the plain pass-through copy therefore
// copies the buffer onto itself, which emulators can show as flickering tiles
// (seen in Ryujinx on RDNA4). Since the color buffer already holds the
// unfiltered frame, the FXAA case jumps to the jump table's default case and
// draws nothing. The wrapper (sub_71021A3974) also skips refreshing the
// temporal history buffer for FXAA, as it does for SMAA, since nothing reads it.

@enabled
021A39F4 1F791E72   // TST W8, #~2          (was CMP W8, #2: no history buffer for types 0 and 2)
021A3E70 F2FFFF17   // B def_71021A3DA0     (was MOV X0, X21 = FXAA case entry)
@stop

// Same agl/gsys FilterAA as Splatoon 2; the constructor and draw dispatch were
// re-derived in main.i64 for this build and byte-verified, not offset-guessed.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
